==============================================================================
GARRISONOS MULTI-EDITION LICENSING MANIFEST
==============================================================================

Copyright (c) 2026 GarrisonOS Project Owners and Contributors.
Project Repository: https://github.com/garrisonos/GarrisonOS
Contact & Inquiries: support@garrisonos.org

GarrisonOS is engineered as a modular, multi-edition property management
platform. The licensing of individual components, modules, distributions, and
build targets is manifest-driven and governed by the declarations in each
module's `module.json` manifest and the root `editions.json` manifest.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0. MODULE-LEVEL LICENSE DECLARATIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every module residing under the `modules/` directory explicitly specifies its
governing license and edition classification within its `module.json` manifest:
- `"license"`: Defines the governing legal license (e.g. `AGPL-3.0-or-later` or
  `GarrisonOS-Fair-Code-1.0`).
- `"edition"`: Declares the minimum edition tier (`community`, `standard`, or
  `enterprise`).

When isolating, reusing, or redistributing an individual module independently of
the whole repository, the specific license declared in that module's `module.json`
shall govern.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. GARRISONOS COMMUNITY EDITION (GNU AGPLv3)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The GarrisonOS Community Edition consists of the open-source core platform
and all baseline modules developed through Core Alpha (including properties,
contacts, leases, attachments, accounting, maintenance, conversations, and
backup) when compiled, packaged, or executed under the Community Edition
runtime target (`GARRISON_EDITION=community` or `npm run package:community`).

The Community Edition is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License,
Version 3 (AGPLv3), as published by the Free Software Foundation.
The complete license text is available in LICENSE.AGPL.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. GARRISONOS STANDARD EDITION (FAIR-CODE)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The GarrisonOS Standard Edition is the primary official distribution, packaged
release, and container image for property management operations. It is governed
by the GarrisonOS Fair-Code License v1.0 (see LICENSE.FAIRCODE):

- FREE TIER: Free for production use for up to fifty (50) managed units.
- GRACE PERIOD: A ten (10) unit grace window (51 to 60 units) is permitted.
- COMMERCIAL LICENSE: Portfolios exceeding sixty (60) units require a paid
  Commercial License from the Project Owners.
- SaaS RESTRICTION: Providing the Software as a hosted service or commercial
  Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) to third parties is strictly prohibited.
- TELEMETRY: Standard Edition incorporates a periodic heartbeat and update check
  to updates.garrisonos.org.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. GARRISONOS ENTERPRISE EDITION (COMMERCIAL)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The GarrisonOS Enterprise Edition is licensed under commercial enterprise
terms for high-scale portfolios and institutions. It provides:
- Custom unit limits (e.g., 500, 2,500, unlimited).
- Air-gapped and private VPC operation via an Ed25519-signed offline cryptographic
  license key, requiring zero outbound network calls or telemetry.
- Commercial indemnity and dedicated support agreements.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. RESTRICTION ON CROSS-LICENSE EXTRACTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modules and source files governed by the GarrisonOS Fair-Code License or
Enterprise terms are proprietary works of the Project Owners. You may NOT
extract, backport, bundle, re-license, or incorporate any portion of Fair-Code
or Enterprise code into the Community Edition, nor into any open-source fork
or distribution governed by AGPL, GPL, MIT, Apache, or any other open-source
license, without prior written authorization from the Project Owners.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. USER INTERFACE ATTRIBUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pursuant to Section 7(b) of AGPLv3 and Section 5 of the Fair-Code License,
all interactive, graphical, or web-facing deployments across all editions must
prominently display the text "Powered by GarrisonOS" linking to
https://github.com/garrisonos/GarrisonOS in the main navigation or footer.

For licensing inquiries, commercial keys, or enterprise support, please contact:
support@garrisonos.org
